data.content:
## What breaks in .NET 11

**Sync I/O on the Cosmos DB provider is fully removed — no opt-in, no workaround.** In .NET 10 you could re-enable it; in EF Core 11 every synchronous call (`ToList()`, `First()`, `Count()`, `SaveChanges()`) **always throws**.

### Fix: convert to async

```csharp
public class ProductRepository
{
    private readonly CosmosDbContext _context;

    public async Task<List<Product>> GetAllAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.ToListAsync();
    }

    public async Task<Product> GetByIdAsync(int id)
    {
        return await _context.Products.FirstAsync(p => p.Id == id);
    }

    public async Task<int> GetCountAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.CountAsync();
    }

    public async Task SaveAsync(Product product)
    {
        _context.Products.Add(product);
        await _context.SaveChangesAsync();
    }
}
```

All callers must be updated to `await` these methods. There is no configuration switch to restore the old sync-over-async behavior — it's a permanent removal.

**Also note** (since you use Cosmos): owned collections with no items now return an **empty collection** instead of `null`. Update any `is null` checks to `.Count == 0`.
